    {
      "id": 231256,
      "name": "catDreaming",
      "username": "catDreaming",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/4491bb/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2020-07-11T15:54:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Adding durability to a lieutenant feels counterproductive.</p>\n<p>Your sample d10 Leiutenant will take a minimum of 3~4 hits to take normally. Having them reset to a d10 post defeat once pushes that up to anywhere from 6~8 attacks at minimum.</p>\n<p>For contrast, a d12 Leiutenant will take a minimum of 4~5 hits to take down normally, only one fewer than the reviving d10. You can then throw on something like +2 or +3 to Leiutenant damage saves, and get something that will likely take far longer to fell than the reviving d10 Lieutenant with a minimum of modification.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I need to run the numbers on that quick.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:06:28.882Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
